WEBVTT

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.640
Shinjuurou...

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.950
I'm at my limit...

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.970
Bettennou!

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.840
Bettennou-sama!

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:12.440
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:19.030
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:24.450
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.870
Things never get any better.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.790
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:38.090
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:43.560
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:49.310
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:55.440
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:01.200
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.160
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.500
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:13.090
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:19.590
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.470
I thought you said that Kaishou wasn't on any of the TV station's cameras...

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.690
That's how Diet Member Kuramitsu
told us to respond to that question...

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:35.940
This was sent to us.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.400
Does this mean Kaishou Rinroku is still alive?

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.080
Yes, that is certainly what my father said.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.950
I was at home, wasn't I?

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.000
How long do you plan to keep talking about this?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.650
Please, leave already.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.960
Wait, Mr. Detective!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.990
Did you receive one of these as well?

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:01.810
Did the hospital provide Kaishou's DNA for verifying his remains?

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:03.720
No.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.930
She took it from my father's brush.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.040
That's right, selfishness!

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.440
If solar power generation was nationalised,

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.820
Kaishou Rinroku would no longer be able to increase his profits...

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.820
...from the power production method he had established.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.820
But now he has passed on.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.320
Perhaps this is divine punishment?

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.940
Our generation can prepare an environment of solar power and smart grid infrastructure,

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.080
making Japan the world leader in renewable energy!

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.840
Oh, you mean this?

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:39.590
I don't think there's any point in trying to attend, but... I wanted to check...

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.070
But I do wonder who pulled this prank...

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.340
Maybe it was Kaishou Rinroku's ghost!

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.550
Milady!

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.730
I tried to stop her, but...

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.730
Your father has most certainly passed on...

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.740
That's why I want to know who's posing as my father.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.240
This joke is in terrible taste;

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.620
TV is always like this...

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.620
...summoning victims to the scene of a crime!

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.030
We're not doing a show here!

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.660
I was summoned as well.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:21.300
"You are invited to a party in which the real
criminal behind the bombing will be revealed."

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.360
W-Why are you here?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.670
Did you set all this up?!

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.580
You too?!

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.250
Come now, everyone!

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.690
Shouldn't we be taking our seats?

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.060
The party is about to begin.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.970
Defeated Detective!

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.770
After bringing about Chairman Kaishou's death,

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.510
you still insist on such mockery?

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.530
I was summoned here as well.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.160
In other words, a crime is going to occur.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:51.660
A major crime...

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.930
What do you mean a "major crime"?!

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.080
Kaishou tried to kill us,

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.120
and when everyone found out, he killed himself!

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.090
The crime has long occurred-

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.430
They're real.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.140
What does my father...

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:15.360
...I mean, what does the organiser of this party want?

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.500
Who knows?

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.270
But consider this:

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:22.320
Revenge against the person who framed Kaishou Rinroku.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.990
Revenge?!

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.000
Are we expected to use these weapons to kill one another...

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.610
...until the real criminal is found?!

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.410
If that's the case, you should definitely be the first one to die!

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.440
I admit that my deductions were mistaken...

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.460
...in good faith, of course.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.400
What are you saying?

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.180
When the explosion happened here,

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.500
the real Kaishou-shi was at home,

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.100
and the one who appeared at the TV station was an impostor.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.470
It was all governed by the power of Bettennou.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:50.340
That's what I had reasoned...

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.760
No... That's what I was made to believe.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:54.520
Yuuki Shinjuurou will certainly infer the presence of Bettennou.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.640
He's a great detective, after all.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.700
Kaishou had obtained Bettennou.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:00.850
In order to make me believe this,

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:04.070
someone went through the trouble of making Kaishou appear before a family member.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:08.150
The fact that this very family member possesses a
personality incapable of telling lies was also part of the plan.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.720
Wait! Then...

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.790
That's why I'm saying my initial deduction was incorrect.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:18.250
The Kaishou Rinroku-shi that came to the TV station was the real one...

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.580
...and the Kaishou you saw at your home was the true culprit,

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.830
posing as Kaishou through the power of Bettennou.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.380
What is this Bettennou you keep talking about-

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.800
Please, just think of it as a powerful form of hypnotism.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:34.300
Where is your proof that the Kaishou at the TV station was the real one?

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.390
The surveillance camera footage.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:40.660
If the Kaishou that appeared at the TV
station was using the power of Bettennou,

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.060
there's no way he would have been there when I watched the recording days later.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.940
But I did see him. Undoubtedly.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.060
It's been a while since I've taken the train;

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.740
I had no idea where to transfer.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.800
We accompanied him yesterday to the TV studio, but...

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:52.830
...I never thought something like this could happen.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:57.050
I thought you said that the fact their stories contradicted one another...

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.430
...was proof that Kaishou-san hadn't been at the TV station!

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:01.450
There's a simple answer.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.300
One of them was lying.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:08.460
Fuwa-san. I expect you heard what Chairman Kaishou said at the time.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.850
Now that you mention it, I remember him saying something about coming by train...

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:15.110
If so, that would make Mizuno the one who was lying.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:18.970
But why would Mizuno bother to tell a lie that would hurt Chairman Kaishou?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.440
Because Mizuno was part of Full Circle.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.980
Mizuno knew things that he had no way of knowing otherwise.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:31.490
It seems you achieved a rare victory with Yajima-san's case...

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:33.270
He knew about a case that he shouldn't have known existed, unless...

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.620
...but don't let it go to your head!

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:35.740
...he was a prosecutor or had access to Kaishou's private records.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:41.530
There was a rumour that Commander Mizuno was insisting on having a full-access key from many major companies,

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.380
stating that it was necessary for security.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.630
Was Mizuno-san the culprit?

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:48.210
A missile...

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:50.830
There were reports of a rocket launcher being found on site...

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:53.010
...that was the same type as the Public Defense Force's.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.010
If it was fired from the water nearby,

00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:00.250
it would be too close for the Self-Defense Force to even detect it.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:04.980
The way you say that makes it sounds like you've already checked the armoury.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:08.270
It is possible that he took one from there.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:18.580
The only other possibility is that there was a bomb set within the TV station beforehand.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:24.050
JJ Systems' microwave satellite is still in the experimental stages...

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:26.210
...and has no capability of causing such destruction.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:31.340
So we falsely accused him with incorrect data?!

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:34.130
Yes... With the data you yourself leaked.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.810
Oh my, Mr. Detective!

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.980
Weren't you just saying that Mizuno was the culprit-

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:43.770
I don't remember saying he did it alone.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:48.830
The Public Defense Force may have managed to penetrate the data of major corporations,

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:52.280
but proper authorisation is necessary to access government information.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.480
You're saying that Diet Member
Kuramitsu cooperated with Full Circle?!

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.730
Even though Mizuno was an old friend of yours,

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.410
you took measures to hide it.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:02.620
Not even Diet members are allowed through!

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.150
You have no proof of that!

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.830
But I am certain.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:08.330
This is the handkerchief I lent to you.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.270
It was returned to me by my partner.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.670
Why?

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.470
I ran into him somewhere and gave it to him!

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:17.890
My partner had been missing for a while.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.850
Then he appeared as Inga...

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.060
It's unimaginable that anyone other
than Bettennou could manipulate Inga.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:33.540
In other words, you would have had to have been at the place where my partner was captured...

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.570
...as well as where Bettennou resided.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.770
This is a trap!

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:40.410
<i>This</i> is the conspiracy!

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:41.490
Yuuki Shinjuurou!

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:45.580
You made it seem like Kaishou was alive in order to frame me...!

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.000
Gunshots?!

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:50.110
Who's there?!

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:50.880
Over there?!

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:54.670
He's trying to assault all of us!

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:55.840
Run!

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.350
Hayami-kun!

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:58.930
Don't move!

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:02.500
Is this really Kaishou's revenge?!

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.020
I get it! I'm sorry!

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.030
I spoke badly of you, but you'd been framed!

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.020
Resent me all you want!

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:11.610
I don't resent any of you.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.960
Kaishou Rinroku...

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.570
Father!

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:36.890
I'm sorry, I shouldn't have put you through a memorial service at your young age...

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:40.100
That's not... That's not all you've put me through!

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.750
Chairman...

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.390
Everyone, I'm sorry to have worried you!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.390
I faked my own death in order to escape someone's plot against me.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:54.350
I then waited for whoever was behind that plot to make a move.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:57.650
Just as I thought, he put together this farce...

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.220
He?

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:01.630
Isn't that right, my little Defeated Detective?

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:03.500
What are you trying to accomplish?

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.730
I'm merely searching for the truth.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:07.830
I'd like you to tell me what your true objective is.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:12.660
Everyone, this is his partner...

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.920
...but he's no ordinary partner.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:22.610
A monster!

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:26.350
As you can now see, this is not a human, but a monster.

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:29.650
Up until now, the Defeated Detective had been using this monster...

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:32.990
...to tear apart people's hearts as he pleased.

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:35.480
Today, he will receive his retribution.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:38.520
Stop it...

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:42.010
Tell me... What is your true objective?

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.110
Stop it...

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.270
What is it you wish for?

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:46.630
Father... That's enough!

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:47.760
There's nothing I can do...

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:52.410
...people have no choice but to answer what she asks.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.580
Just one question...

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.960
Answer me... What is it you wish for?

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.000
Stop it...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.770
That's enough, Inga.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:05.350
I answered your question long ago.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:06.550
Ask me! Inga!

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.220
What are you seeing right now?

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.180
Rain and... Yuuko...

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:10.890
Only you!

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:16.100
Therefore, I'll never have to answer your questions again.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.980
I know what happened to you.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.500
Bettennou is a god, so you can't resist her.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:22.990
That's probably what you were told.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:26.150
I'm going to disprove that now.

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:27.870
Bettennou is no god!

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.060
Stop it!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.120
The fact that you've been using that monster still stands!

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:35.120
Bettennou makes the words of her master appear to be reality,

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:42.190
but those illusions cannot extend to those unable to see or hear you.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.760
Also, for instance, if the actual person is there before you,

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.260
you would be unable to masquerade as them.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:50.900
Shinjuurou... You knew, didn't you?

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:53.270
Yeah. Ever since he appeared.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:57.770
In my eyes, you look like nothing more
than someone trying to mimic Kaishou...

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.900
...Hayami Seigen.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.900
Hayami-san? What are you saying?

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:05.780
I thought Hayami-kun fell through the floor...

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:10.510
If Kaishou hadn't obtained Bettennou, it had to be you.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.080
You probably shot Kazamori out of precaution,

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.100
after seeing the electric shock she used while we were at the prison.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.040
But it was a wasted effort.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.160
What are you...

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:18.170
...talking about?

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:19.800
I've been trying to tell you:

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:24.000
since I've had the real Kaishou Rinroku right before my eyes this whole time,

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.940
even if an impersonator were to show up,

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.300
my brain couldn't be fooled.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.100
The real...?

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:32.360
You're stupider than I thought, Mr. National Police Agency.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.680
He's not the only one responsible.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.780
H-Hey! Now's not the time!

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:41.280
You cannot remove a god from within man.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.690
But by showing reverence to something that's considered to be a god,

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:49.680
you make it into one, enabling you to force it on the people at large.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:53.990
Hayami-kun, this is precisely what you did.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:57.540
Chairman?!

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:06.960
Hayami-kun...

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.340
...what is the meaning of this?!

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:12.620
Using the power of Bettennou, he impersonated me.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.350
Well enough to fool even Rie.

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.160
That's why I made it look like I died...

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:21.000
...so as not to give power to the person posing as me.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.110
I helped the Chairman.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:26.940
That day, the chairman gave the
appearance that he was getting in the car,

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.490
then he mixed in with the rest of my force.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:36.670
He then disguised himself as AD from the television station and left the scene.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:42.790
The corpse found in the car was the body of the collapsed man that had been carried to the hospital days before.

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:48.170
The DNA matched because some of that corpse's hair had been attached to your brush.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.630
But... That brush was...

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:54.550
You knew that Father was safe as well?!

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:57.810
Inga, do you still see Bettennou as a god?

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:02.460
She's merely a misbegotten soul.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.940
Specifically, a "spirit of words".

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:10.850
Formerly, the words "victory" and "kamikaze" were unleashed by the statesmen of this country.

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:13.570
They sent us off to war, instilling the belief that they were gods...

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:16.910
...in order to make things that didn't even exist seem real.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.210
If it's a soul, then it happens to be my favourite food...

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:22.420
...misbegotten or not!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.580
Using this, you pretended to panic, masqueraded as Kaishou,

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.780
and tried to make me confess.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.390
That's what you planned, at least.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.370
You saw right through me, huh?

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:10.170
Full Circle's Mizuno and Kuramitsu were
trying to find a way to prosecute JJ Systems.

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:14.390
After obtaining Bettennou, you approached them.

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:17.890
I haven't done anything wrong!

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:21.810
I tried to take down that self-serving Kaishou Rinroku for the betterment of Japan!

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:23.310
Is that so?

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:26.580
You were trying to prevent the
nationalisation of solar power generation!

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.710
Since you were trying to break into that field yourself!

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:32.650
The field I'm entering is solar thermal energy.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:33.700
What's the difference?!

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:37.700
Your inability to make that distinction is where your limits lie.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.830
The era may come when we can provide the proper technology...

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:43.310
...to countries that have vast deserts and receive strong sunlight,

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.480
to achieve the means to build solar thermal power plants...

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.600
...and carry that electricity via HVDC transmissions,

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:53.220
or collaborate with other countries to send microwave transmissions from space.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:56.490
What?! How could we rely on other countries for electricity?!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:57.760
It's a dream, of course.

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:01.220
But some day the borders between countries will disappear.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:04.020
That's the kind of dream I have.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:23.080
You've been giving me a taste bit by bit... Now I'm really hungry!

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:39.690
I suppose I can understand that Kuramitsu took the
conspiracy theories seriously and wanted to frame Kaishou...

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:42.100
...but Hayami, what was it you were after?

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:49.070
Don't make this monster ask me...

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:50.360
How rude...

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:54.440
It was you, Prosecutor Koyama.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.000
Me? What do you mean?!

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:02.200
Figures... You never saw anyone other than Kaishou Rinroku with those eyes.

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:06.960
To you, Kaishou was practically... a god.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.830
I wanted you to revere me that way.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:11.400
Hayami-san...

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:15.700
But it was foolish of me to try to become a god.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:24.310
You!

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.600
It wasn't me.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.180
Bettennou said this:

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.670
"Live. Fall."

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:35.570
Go.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:44.880
I wondered what I was going to do if you hadn't recognised the song.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.630
That was a song from Yonagahime 3+1.

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:49.370
That member's death was fictional.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:51.950
In other words, you weren't dead either.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.880
I can't even call that a deduction.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.590
And how did you know that I was dressed as AD?

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:02.090
I confirmed the location of the real AD before entering the studio.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:04.030
As expected!

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:06.970
Father! We can give Mr. Detective a ride too, can't we?

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.980
What do you say? If you'd like, you can join us for dinner, or-

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:14.150
Come on, Father, hurry up!

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:16.480
There's one thing I forgot to say.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:21.740
About Mizuno, who died in your fake suicide.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:25.280
There's no way that Mizuno would have cooperated with your plot...

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:29.120
...so being, he must have been dead before the explosion.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:36.080
The reason you went with such a flashy form of suicide was also to cover up the cause of Mizuno's death.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:37.130
I was...

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.840
I was the one who killed him.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.130
I wonder.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:47.890
Even if that is the truth, Kaishou, you admitted to disposing of Mizuno before he was tried by law.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:49.950
Why?

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:55.770
Was it because Mizuno, who was part of Full Circle, had even more information about you?

00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:00.630
Earlier, you talked about solar thermal power plants.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:05.660
As compensation for the recent war, the government has offered to supply technology to other countries.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:09.540
You saw all this coming far ahead and
cooperated during the war in order to-

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:13.290
Stop it, Shinjuurou...

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.120
Please...

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:22.920
If all humans were saints and sages, all truths would be laid bare,

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:26.810
and every great cause, justification, means, ideal, and lie...

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:29.220
...would likely become unnecessary.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:32.840
But I wonder if that day will ever come.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:40.330
All we can do is improve ourselves, little by little.

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:41.480
You're wrong.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.820
People fall.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.740
They lay bare the true essence within themselves, their souls.

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:51.310
They want for beauty; they seek luxury and pleasure.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:55.370
But at the same time, they love what's right just as much.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:57.630
With all the evils that exist, there are just as many justices.

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:01.360
I want to love people.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.770
I want to know the beauty of that.

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:05.040
For that purpose...

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:08.340
...I will expose souls.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.100
What a shame...

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:15.730
I look forward to what lies ahead.

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:37.460
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.240
What did you call me all the way out here for?

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:36.070
I had something I forgot to tell you.

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:38.340
Surely you just want to insult my father more!

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:45.420
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:45.470
You were right.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:53.100
We're seeking the (truth), "We don't even care if it's a lie";

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.590
I have something that I've yet to show you.

00:21:48.730 --> 00:21:50.110
Will you listen?

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:50.890
Yeah.

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:57.390
As if we can see right through it,

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:57.100
A woman saved my life once.

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:01.730
We'd only just met, and there was no benefit to her in saving me...

00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:01.440
We follow it along.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:05.400
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:07.400
She died... And Inga's body... is hers.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:09.410
Like a falling feather.

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:11.150
That's why I decided to stay with him...

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:12.530
Looking for, find it,

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:18.870
So we can come closer together.

00:22:33.390 --> 00:22:37.390
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:41.400
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:44.480
Looking for, find it,

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:49.320
So we can come closer together.
